# Gate-authority policy (process.md §4; process-options.md "Gate authority
# levels"). One value on the last line — who approves a gate advance:
#   attended      — a human approves each gate (the default; standard §4).
#   single-ratify — LLM-gate review through G1+G2; the human ratifies the
#                   queued decisions once at G2 close; autonomous rules after.
#   autonomous    — every gate except G-Final closes on an independent
#                   fresh-context LLM reviewer's recorded verdict.
# A non-default level is amended into the repo by the deviation register
# (docs/gate-policy.md — scaffolded by `bootstrap.py --gate-policy`); the §4
# fixed points hold at every level. Change this value in a reviewed commit,
# like docs/gate.
attended
